<title>USA: Fed approves Mellon takeover of consulting firm.</title>
<headline>Fed approves Mellon takeover of consulting firm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve said on Monday that it approved a proposal by Mellon Bank Corp of Pittsburgh to take over Buck Consultants Inc of New York and then to offer employee benefits consulting services.</p>
<p>Mellon has assets of $42.7 billion and is the 22nd largest bank in the United States. Buck provides employee consulting services worldwide and has about 5,000 clients ranging from multinational corporations to health care providers.</p>
</text>
